{"context": "published", "host": "www.josephsmithpapers.org", "showHeader": true, "footerStyle": "mini", "statusCode": 200, "uri": "egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a", "page": "8", "is404": false, "gallery": [{"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_001_thumb.jpg", "page": "1", "label": "[1]", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/1"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_001-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "2", "label": "[0]", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/2"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_002_thumb.jpg", "page": "3", "label": "2", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/3"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_002-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "4", "label": "[0]", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/4"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_003_thumb.jpg", "page": "5", "label": "3", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/5"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_003-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "6", "label": "[0]", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/6"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_004_thumb.jpg", "page": "7", "label": "4", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/7"}, {"image": "/8102/8102_ms1295_0_04_eajs_005_thumb.jpg", "page": "8", "label": "[5]", "href": "/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a/8"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-a", "series": "JSPPR", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPR6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppr6-sub04", "documentSeriesTitle": "Egyptian Alphabet, circa Early July–circa November 1835–A", "editorialPageNumber": "5", "isPageNumberPresent": false, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/53991849/53991849-0008.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X75354\"> </td><td xml:id=\"X75355\"><span class=\"icon-glyph\">✦</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">5.28</span>]</td><td xml:id=\"X75357\">In the first degree Ah-broam—signifies The father of the faithful, the first right, the elders second degree—same sound—A follower of rightiousness— Third degree—same sound—One who possesses great Knowledge— Fourth degree—same sound—A follower of righteousness, a possessor of greater Knowledge. Fifth degree—Ah-bra-oam. The father of many nations, a prince of peace, one who keeps the commandments of God, a patriarch, a rightful heir, a high priest.</td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X75360\"><span class=\"underscore\">W</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12254869550351948220\"><a href=\"#12254869550351948220\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans13\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This letter and the letter written after the explanation are written in blue ink in unidentified handwriting.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X75362\"> </td><td xml:id=\"X75363\"> </td></tr> </tbody></table> <div class=\"right wasptag\"><span class=\"underscore\">W</span> [<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">remainder of verso blank</span>] [p. [5]]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span><table width=\"100%\"> <tbody><tr> <td xml:id=\"X75354\"> </td><td xml:id=\"X75355\"><span class=\"icon-glyph\">✦</span><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>[<span class=\"josephswriting\">5.28</span>]<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15136218928116495253\"><a href=\"#15136218928116495253\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans58\"><span id=\"documenttrans58\">58</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: Character possibly inscribed by <a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Oliver Cowdery</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td><td xml:id=\"X75357\">In the first degree Ah-broam—signifies The father of the faithful, the first right, the elders second <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>degree—same sound—A follower of <span class=\"deleted\">sig</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16732802852850358525\"><a href=\"#16732802852850358525\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans59\"><span id=\"documenttrans59\">59</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: It is possible this “<span class=\"deleted\">sig</span>” is a copying error from “signifies” above. The presence of other potential copying errors (e.g., “<span class=\"deleted\">of</span> Knowledge”, below) may indicate that <a href=\"/person/oliver-cowdery\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Cowdery</a> copied this entry from a nonextant source.</p><hr></div></div></aside> rightiousness— Third degree—same sound—One who possesses great <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Knowledge— Fourth degree—same sound—A follower of righteousness, a possessor of greater <span class=\"deleted\">of</span> Knowledge. <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Fifth degree—Ah-bra-oam. The father of many nations, a prince of peace, one who keeps the command<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>ments of God, a patriarch, a rightful heir, a high priest.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12534416466379667869\"><a href=\"#12534416466379667869\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans60\"><span id=\"documenttrans60\">60</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">TEXT: This explanation is significantly expanded from the previous version in this document and the version in <a href=\"/paper-summary/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-c\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/egyptian-alphabet-circa-early-july-circa-november-1835-c\" poptitle=\"Egyptian Alphabet, circa Early July–circa November\n 1835–C\">Egyptian Alphabet–C</a>. The explanation employs a system of degrees similar to the one found in the <a href=\"/paper-summary/grammar-and-alphabet-of-the-egyptian-language-circa-july-circa-november-1835/8\" class=\"externalLink\">Grammar and Alphabet</a> volume, and the explanation also correlates with the explanations found in that volume.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> </tr> <tr> <td xml:id=\"X75360\">&lt;​<span class=\"underscore\">W</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17899206140996123786\"><a href=\"#17899206140996123786\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans13\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This letter and the letter written after the explanation are written in blue ink in unidentified handwriting.</p><hr></div></div></aside></td> <td xml:id=\"X75362\"> </td><td xml:id=\"X75363\"> </td></tr> </tbody></table> <div class=\"right wasptag\">&lt;​<span class=\"underscore\">W</span>​&gt; [<span class=\"italic note-data editorial-comment\" isnote=\"Y\">remainder of verso blank</span>] [p. [5]]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [],